{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-10-1","title":"Job 10:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job, taking liberty of complaint, expostulates with God about his afflictions. 18 He complains of life, and craves a little ease before death.</p>\n<p>My soul. 3:20-23; 6:8,9; 5:15,16,20; 9:21; 14:13; Nu 11:15; 1Ki 19:4 Jon 4:3,8 is weary of my life. or, cut off while I live. I willleave. 7:11; 19:4; 21:2-4 I will speak. 15,16; 6:2-4,26; 7:11; 16:6-16; Ps 32:3-5; Isa 38:15,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-2","title":"Job 10:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Do not. Ps 6:1-4; 25:7; 38:1-8; 109:21; 143:2; Ro 8:1 shew me. 8:5,6; 34:31,32; Ps 139:23,24; La 3:40-42; 5:16,17; 1Co 11:31,32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-3","title":"Job 10:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Is it good. 34:5-7,18,19; 36:7-9,17,18; 40:2,8; La 3:2-18 despise. Ps 69:33 the work. Heb. the labour. 14:15; 34:19; Ps 138:8; Isa 64:8; 1Pe 4:19 shine upon. 8:20; Jer 12:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-4","title":"Job 10:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>seest thou. 9:32; 1Sa 16:7; Lu 16:15; Re 1:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-5","title":"Job 10:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Ps 90:2-4; 102:12,24-27; Heb 1:12; 2Pe 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-6","title":"Job 10:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>14-17; Ps 10:15; 44:21; Jer 2:34; Zep 1:12; Joh 2:24,25; 1Co 4:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-7","title":"Job 10:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Thou knowest. Heb. It is upon thy knowledge. 23:10; 31:6,14,35; 42:7; Ps 1:6; 7:3,8,9; 17:3; 26:1-5 Ps 139:1,2,21-24; Joh 21:17; 2Co 1:12; 1Th 2:10 and there. 23:13,14; De 32:39; Ps 50:22; Da 3:15; Ho 2:10; Joh 10:28-30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-8","title":"Job 10:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>hands. Ps 119:73; Isa 43:7 have made me. Heb. took pains about me. yet thou. 3; Ge 6:6,7; Jer 18:3-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-9","title":"Job 10:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Remember. 7:7; Ps 25:6,7,18; 89:47; 106:4 thou hast. Ge 2:7; 3:19; Isa 45:9; 64:8; Jer 18:6 into dust again. 17:14; Ps 22:15; 90:3; Ec 12:7; Ro 9:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-10","title":"Job 10:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>poured. Ps 139:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-11","title":"Job 10:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>clothed. 2Co 5:2,3 fenced. Heb. hedged. 40:17,18; Eze 37:4-8; Eph 4:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-12","title":"Job 10:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>life and favour. Ge 19:19; Mt 6:25; Ac 17:25,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-13","title":"Job 10:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>hid. 23:9; Ec 8:6,7; Isa 45:15; Ro 11:33 I know. 23:13; De 32:39; Isa 45:7; 46:9-11; La 3:37; Eph 3:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-14","title":"Job 10:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>then. 13:26,27; 14:16; Ps 130:3; 139:1 thou wilt. 7:21; Ex 34:7; Nu 14:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-15","title":"Job 10:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>If I be wicked. 7; 9:29; 27:7; Ps 9:17; Isa 3:11; 6:5; Mal 3:18; Ro 2:8,9 righteous. 9:12,15,20,21; Isa 64:5,6; Lu 17:10 I am full. 21:6; 23:15 see. Ex 3:7; Ps 25:18; 119:153; La 1:20; 5:1-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-16","title":"Job 10:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Thou huntest. Isa 38:13; La 3:10; Ho 13:7,8; Am 3:8 marvellous. Nu 16:29,30; De 28:59</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-17","title":"Job 10:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>witnesses. that is, plagues. 16:8; Ru 1:21 changes.I am as if attacked by successive troops; if one company be wearied, another succeeds to the attack.</p>\n<p>Ps 55:19; Jer 48:11; Zep 1:12 war. 16:11-16; 19:6-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-18","title":"Job 10:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>hast thou. 3:10,11; Jer 15:10; 20:14-18; Mt 26:24 given up. 11:20; 14:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-19","title":"Job 10:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Ps 58:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-20","title":"Job 10:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>my days few. 7:6,7,16; 8:9; 9:25,26; 14:1; Ps 39:5; 103:15,16 cease. 7:17-21; 13:21; Ps 39:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-21","title":"Job 10:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>I go whence. 7:8-10; 14:10-14; 2Sa 12:23; 14:14; Isa 38:11 the land. 3:5; Ps 88:6,11,12 the shadow. 3:5; Ps 23:4; Jer 2:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-10-22","title":"Job 10:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>the shadow of death.Where death projects his shadow, intercepting the light of life: without any order, having no arrangement, no distinction of inhabitants; the poor and the rich are there, the king and the beggar, their bodies in equal corruption and disgrace: where the light is as darkness, a palpable obscure, space and place, with only such a light or capability of distinction, as renders \"darkness visible.\"</p>\n<p>3:5; 34:22; 38:17; Ps 23:4; 44:19; 88:12; Jer 2:6; 13:16; Lu 16:26</p>"}]}